0-F	Instructions, no args included

These are followed by a marker ID:

10	mark	Set the marker to the current instruction location relative to the origin of the instruction segment.
11	rel	Emit the difference between the current instruction location and the marker.
12	absi	Emit the absolute location for the marker.

These are followed by a literal constant:	

13	const	Emit a literal constant.
14	absd	Emit the absolute data address given the offset from the data segment.

Interface variables:

code_string	Pointer to array of code. Code modified by packer.
code_length	Length of code_string, modified by packer.

code_markers	Pointer to array of markers. Markers modified by packer.

i_seg_base	Base of instruction segment
d_seg_base	Base of data segment



p;csp :variable		# code string pointer
p;ncr :variable		# words remaining in code string
p;final :variable	# allow p$emit to work

p$finish : 1 p;final ! p$pass
p$scan : 0 p;final ! p$pass &repeat
packer : code_string @ p;csp ! code_length @ p;ncr ! p$scan p$finish